#1029 is fixed and committed as fde3f1ba. Build, clippy, fmt check and cargo test all pass (6237 unit tests plus every integration suite, 0 failures), and tests/harness_logic.sh is 203/0. I couldn't run a live model stream, so the evidence is the tests.

What changed in `src/format/markdown.rs`:
• **Headings:** the `#` marker is gone in colour mode, and so is an optional closing `##`. Bold inside a heading now renders, and the heading's style comes back after each bold span. With colour off, every style is empty, so the # stays as the only sign it's a heading; a test covers both modes. Lines like #tag or seven #s aren't headings and render as before, and a test pins that.
• **List and quote prefixes:** when `-`, `1.` or `>` is followed in the same delta by an opening `**`, the `**` is now held until its closing pair arrives, as text in the middle of a line already was (#661). This fixes all three splits named in the issue.
• **Blockquote defect (d):** I fixed this one too instead of filing it. `>` now waits one more character so the optional space is dropped, the same way a whole line drops it, and the italic is closed at the end of the line. Nothing was left over, so no new issue.

Before/after bytes:
• `"## The **apply step"`: before `\e[1m\e[36m## The apply** step\e[0m, after \e[1m\e[36mThe \e[1mapply\e[0m\e[1m\e[36m step\e[0m`
• `["- ","apply: x\n"]: before \e[36m•\e[0m apply: x, after \e[36m•\e[0m \e[1mapply\e[0m: x`

New `src/format/markdown_parity_tests.rs`: it renders each fixture whole, line by line, one character at a time and through the exact splits from the issue, and checks the full output strings are identical. It also checks that the fixtures really contain the # and ** being tested, and that no # or ** leaks outside code. One exception: per-character streaming inside a code fence dims each piece separately by design (#147), so that case compares the visible text rather than the bytes.

Things you might not expect:
• **Four existing tests changed:** they expected headings to keep their #. I changed their expected values on purpose, each with a #1029 comment; no test was deleted.
• **A file outside the task list:** to keep `markdown.rs` inside its size budget, I moved its first block of basic tests unchanged into the new file. That brought it to 3152 lines, under its 3177 entry. The size check then asked me to lower the entry to 3152, so I edited tests/module_size.rs.
• **A rename:** the new test module is named `markdown_parity_tests`, because the orphan-file check matches modules by file name and failed on my first name, `parity_tests`.

Check that the new tests catch the bug: I switched the list path back to the old renderer, with a NEUTERED marker on that line. Four parity tests failed, naming the ["- **", "apply**: x\n"] split. After restoring it they pass again, and no marker is left in the file.

I added a CHANGELOG line under Unreleased and a note in ARCHITECTURE.md. The commit title says "Fixes #1029", so the issue will close when this is pushed.
